<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The floppy bot: the original's Bot body as a participant its environment
  invokes (environments/room/room.scx, decision D102). It owns the bot
  lifecycle and processing turns; its abilities are invoked children
  (decision D6: invoke lifecycle replaces the original's attachment protocol).

    live { activating -> active { unfocused, focused, processing,
      cancelling_processing } }
    live -bot.deactivate-> deactivating -> inactive (final)
    live -bot.reboot (the cognition asks for one)-> live (re-entered:
      every ability is cancelled and invoked again)
    activating -bot.deactivate-> deactivating (the original's activation_cancelling)
    cancelling_processing -cancel timeout-> degraded (a final sink)

  Joining (decision D107): the environment's <invoke> is the original's
  attach. Its <param>s are the activation settings (model, bounds, traits,
  database, environment: the environment's id), and the body starts in
  live and activates at once; nothing sends bot.activate. inactive is a
  top-level final state: a failed activation and bot.deactivate end the
  session there, which is its leave; rejoining is the environment invoking
  it again.

  Abilities: live holds <invoke id="cognition">, <invoke
  id="communication"> (abilities/communication/communication.scx, which holds the
  conversation and speaking), <invoke id="identity">
  (abilities/identity/identity.scx, the bot's name), <invoke id="listening">
  (abilities/listening/listening.scx, the ear), <invoke id="stm">
  (abilities/stm/stm.scx, the short-term register, the original's
  bot.register) and <invoke id="persona"> (abilities/persona/persona.scx,
  the owner's traits and the bot's own description of itself); leaving
  live cancels every ability (SCXML
  6.4), which replaces the original's cleanup states: an SCXML invoke cancel is
  synchronous, so there is nothing for the original's 5 min deactivation
  timeout or its reboot preserve/reset cleanup to wait on, and every
  reboot restarts the abilities from their documents (the original's reset). An ability is ready when it
  sends its first bot.ability.offers; the body is active when every
  expected ability is ready. A run-tagged activation timer
  (activation_timeout_ms), an error event, or an ability ending while
  activating fails the activation (bot.activating.failed) and ends the
  session in inactive; an ability ending while active degrades the bot.

  Lifecycle answers (the original's a2cbaa8): the activator is the
  environment that invoked the body, and every terminal goes to it, its
  parent. Every bot.deactivate is answered once: from activating or
  active by bot.deactivated (leaving live cancels the abilities at once,
  so the original's activation_cancelling and its timeout have nothing to
  wait on). The original stamps a terminal with its request's envelope id;
  an SCXML <send> cannot take its id from an expression, and the only
  requester is the parent, so nothing is stamped. The transition into
  degraded on an unacknowledged cancel announces bot.degraded {stage:
  "processing_cancel"}; the original's other stages are cleanups that
  SCXML's synchronous invoke cancel never leaves unfinished, and an
  ability ending while active, which floppy degrades on, has no stage in
  the original, so it ends with its reason only.

  Communication: bot.ability.communication.input from outside, while
  active, goes to the communication, which admits it into its
  conversation; the conversation's text product comes back as
  bot.ability.cognition.input {stimulus}. The communication says a routed
  bot.ability.communication.respond through speaking and answers
  bot.ability.speaking.output or bot.ability.communication.failed, and
  forwards the conversation's bot.ability.conversation.failed and a
  product that is not text, bot.ability.conversation.output, all of
  which the body logs. The same input goes to the identity, which hands
  over bot.ability.cognition.input {stimulus: bot.ability.identity.addressed}
  when the text names the bot, as the cognition hands over a routine's
  bot.behavior.tick (its routines).

  Short-term memory: the body relays a child's bot.ability.memory.stm.turn
  to the register (no child writes turns yet: listening's heard speech
  and the conversation's said messages are the listening and
  communication workstreams' to add), reads the register's recent turns
  (bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns {}) on entering each turn, and
  relays the register's bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.output to the
  cognition. The cognition cannot ask through the body: the request's
  descriptor matches the answer's name too, and scxml.rs judges an
  arriving event by every matching transition's schema, so a body taking
  both would refuse the answer.
  Nothing in floppy reads the register's stimuli yet (the original's
  Learning is not ported), so a bot.ability.memory.stm.recent.output is
  taken and dropped.

  Self: the body relays the cognition's bot.ability.identity.ask to the
  identity and the identity's bot.ability.identity.named (its answer, and
  the name after each adoption) to the cognition, so the cognition can
  tell its own name from a visitor's. It relays the persona's
  bot.ability.persona.output {traits, description} (on waking and after
  each revision written down) to the cognition, which keeps what it was
  last told (the original's Cognition._know_persona).

  Persona (the original's bot.traits, which give a bot a persona): the
  body passes its traits (the activation setting traits, a <param> the
  environment may set; the original's companion example's owner traits by
  default, since the original composes a persona only from traits and
  floppy's body always has one) and its database to the persona. The
  persona's offer (bot.ability.persona.revise) is its readiness but is
  kept out of the turn's choices (turnOffers()): in the original only
  reflection, composed with the same persona, may select a revision.

  Speaking: the communication relays speaking's efference copy,
  bot.ability.speaking.efference (sent on to each Listening ability in
  listening, the original's Speaking listening peers); right after it, the
  communication puts speaking's sound, environment.sound, into the
  environment whose id the body passes it (decision D103, amended
  2026-10-15: the copy reaches the listening first), and the sound comes
  back to the body as any sound there does (the bot hears itself).

  Environment: environment.sound and environment.visual from the
  environment, while active, are first recorded in the short-term
  register (the original's _fan_out_input: bot.ability.memory.stm.record
  {stimulus_name, payload, source?}, the payload the stimulus data's
  bounded scalar projection, <memory:stm_projection>, and source a
  sound's own source, which floppy carries in the sound for the original's
  envelope source; floppy has no envelope id or target to record; a
  one-way message, so registration never blocks admitting the stimulus),
  then go to
  each input ability (input, the original's Bot input: the invoke ids
  of the abilities that perceive raw stimuli; the identity and the
  listening), in
  order, by <foreach>; never to the cognition, which hears of a stimulus
  only as an input ability's product: the listening hands its decoded
  speech or labelled non-speech over as bot.ability.cognition.input, which
  starts a turn like any handoff. The listening's
  bot.ability.listening.failed is logged.

  Turns: bot.input, or an ability's bot.ability.cognition.input handoff
  (the original grants any ability product the turn, blind to its content), in
  unfocused or focused starts a processing turn; the stimulus is the
  envelope {event, data, source} assigned for bot.input (its source null:
  it reaches the body from outside its session, the environment or the
  host), or the handoff's stimulus as given, with the participants its
  producer stamped (none for bot.input: a device report names no one; the
  original's f6c4e08 copies them forward unchanged). The body counts the turn, computes the
  turn's attention bias with <cognition:attention_bias_for_turn> (focus, focus_candidates:
  the original's attention_bias_for_turn from device identity only), assembles the turn's choices (below), sends bot.ability.cognition.input
  {turn, stimulus, focus, focus_candidates, participants, choices} to the cognition, and
  arms bot.processing.timed_out
  (processing_timeout_ms) for the turn. Replies count only when they carry
  the current turn. A timeout sends
  bot.ability.cognition.cancel {turn} and waits in cancelling_processing,
  bounded by processing_timeout_ms clamped to 100..5000 ms (the original's
  cancel wait): the acknowledgement
  fails the turn (bot.processing.failed); no acknowledgement degrades the
  bot. Stimuli that arrive during a turn are held by <event:defer/>
  (scxml.rs namespaces/event) and start the next turns, in order, one per
  return to unfocused or focused, before any later event.

  Choices (the original's per-turn dispatch inventory,
  collect_offered_events): on processing entry the body reads its own
  choices with <decision:choice location="body_choices"
  events="bot.focus_device bot.clear_focus"> (the transitions on active:
  bot.focus_device when the turn has focus candidates, bot.clear_focus when
  a device is focused), <decision:pin> pins bot.focus_device's device to an
  enum of the turn's focus_candidates, and
  <processing:collect_offered_events> tags every choice with the session id
  of the session that offers it (the target a stage sends it to): the
  body's own with its _sessionid, each ability's latest bot.ability.offers
  choices (but the persona's) with the ability's session id (<_sessionid>.<invoke id>, decision
  D110), and, while a device is focused, the events its live session
  accepts, read this turn with <device:snapshot> (decision D109), each
  {event, schema: {type: object}} with the device's id (the device's own
  event:schema decides its data on delivery). Every schema is made
  model-facing ($schema, title and examples dropped); when the choices are
  still over 32 KiB (phase 4 spike (b): a relayed list of 48264 B, with its
  raw message, is over the 96 KiB event bound, so its send raises
  error.execution in the sender) every description is dropped too, and if
  they are still over the turn fails without reaching the cognition.

  Dispatch: the cognition's stages send their own selections, each to the
  session its target names (#_scxml_ + target, decision D104), as the
  original's stages dispatch theirs (cognition.types.dispatch_selected_events):
  a selection of the body's own bot.focus_device or bot.clear_focus reaches
  the body during the turn and is taken by active's transitions, whose
  conds are the original's guards (_ability_selected_configured_focus_device,
  and a clear only while a device is focused). The schemas the generate
  service and the decision service check a selection against (the focus
  device's enum pinned to the turn's candidates, each target an enum of
  the offering sessions) refuse what the original's attention policy
  refused before anything is sent. On the turn's output the body logs
  bot.processing.completed and sends itself the selections that name no
  target: the trusted SpeechHeard seed's bot.ability.communication.input
  (the original dispatches it to a declared event of the bot), which it
  takes as outside communication input.

  Outputs: each event the body emits is sent to its parent, the
  environment, which logs it (decision D102): bot.activated,
  bot.activating.failed, bot.deactivated, bot.processing.completed,
  bot.processing.failed, bot.processing.timed_out,
  bot.processing.cancel.timed_out, bot.degraded, bot.reboot, plus the communication's
  bot.ability.speaking.output, bot.ability.communication.failed,
  bot.ability.conversation.failed and bot.ability.conversation.output, the
  listening's bot.ability.listening.failed, and any ability's
  bot.ability.failed that is not a turn's reply;
  floppy's own records are labelled floppy.* (not the original events):
  floppy.output the turn's selected events (one record per completed turn),
  floppy.choices each turn's choices, and floppy.focus each focus change.

  Contracts: every event the body takes references its one schema file by
  event:schema: its own events in schemas/, and the abilities' events it
  receives in ../../abilities/schemas/. scxml.rs checks them where each event is created: an
  ability's send whose data a schema rejects is not routed and raises
  error.execution in the ability, and an environment's send the schemas
  reject raises error.execution in the environment. No cond asks who sent an
  event: every event name the body takes has one meaning here, whoever
  sends it, so its name and the active state route it. Conds only
  correlate (the turn, the run) and read the focus.

  Running: scx run with an env file and an environment that invokes this
  document (environments/room/room.scx), then bot.input on standard input,
  which the environment gives every bot. The cognition's stages need TYPESAFE_API_KEY (intuition's decision
  service) and FLOPPY_BASE_URL and FLOPPY_API_KEY (reasoning's generate
  service, no default backend); without them a turn fails.

  Time bounds (decision D101): the bounds param may set the cognition's
  child_operation_timeout_ms and child_operation_ceiling_ms (a stage's
  inactivity bound and its backstop) and reflection's revising_timeout_ms
  and revising_ceiling_ms (likewise for a revision through the builder),
  [floppy fields]; the body passes those it was given to the cognition as
  <param name="bounds">, and each one absent is the ability's default
  (README.md, "Defaults").

  Memory (the original's sqlite_memory): the body passes its database (a file in
  the directory the run grants the sql service at /memory, scx run's
  dir option) to the cognition, the communication, the identity and the
  short-term register and the persona as <param name="database">;
  reasoning recalls the cognitive episodes reflection stores, the identity
  its adopted names, the persona the descriptions the bot wrote of itself,
  and the conversation its
  relationship memories (abilities/memory/memory.scx over services/sql, one
  SQLite transaction per invocation). A run without the grant is refused
  before it starts.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:cognition="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/cognition"
       xmlns:decision="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/decision"
       xmlns:device="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/device"
       xmlns:memory="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/memory"
       xmlns:processing="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/processing"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="floppy" initial="live">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- Configuration: the activation settings, which the environment's
         <invoke> may set as <param>s (decision D107). -->
    <data id="model" expr="'Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next'"/>
    <!-- The time bounds for the cognition (its stages' inactivity and
         backstop, and reflection's revising; decision D101): each absent one
         is the ability's own default. -->
    <data id="bounds" expr="({})"/>
    <!-- The memory database file (the original's sqlite_memory
         database), in the directory the run grants the service at /memory. -->
    <data id="database" expr="'/memory/floppy.sqlite'"/>
    <!-- The environment's id (its root's _sessionid, decision D106), which
         the environment gives as a <param>. -->
    <data id="environment" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The owner's traits (the original's bot.traits: one to 24, each at
         most 200 characters), which the environment's <invoke> may set as
         a <param>; by default the original's companion example's
         DEFAULT_TRAITS. -->
    <data id="traits" expr="['warm', 'patient', 'curious', 'honest']"/>
    <data id="activation_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
    <data id="processing_timeout_ms" expr="300000"/>
    <!-- The devices the bot holds, which the environment gives as a
         <param> (decision D105): reference to the device session's
         _sessionid, its address; devices are their references, set on
         each entry into live. -->
    <data id="owned_devices" expr="({})"/>
    <data id="devices" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- This turn's snapshots of the held devices (<device:snapshot>):
         reference to {id, state, attributes, events}. -->
    <data id="device_snapshots" expr="({})"/>
    <!-- The device being read (the <foreach> item). -->
    <data id="device" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Lifecycle: each entry into live is one run; the abilities expected
         and the offers each has sent this run. -->
    <data id="live_run" expr="0"/>
    <data id="expected" expr="['cognition', 'communication', 'identity', 'listening', 'stm', 'persona']"/>
    <data id="offers" expr="({})"/>
    <data id="waiting" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The input abilities each environment.* stimulus fans out to
         (the original's Bot input, as invoke ids), and the one being sent to. -->
    <data id="input" expr="['identity', 'listening']"/>
    <data id="ability" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The admitted stimulus's bounded scalar projection, for the
         short-term register (<memory:stm_projection>). -->
    <data id="stm_payload" expr="({})"/>
    <!-- The Listening abilities that receive speaking's efference copy
         (the original's Speaking listening peers, as invoke ids). -->
    <data id="listening_abilities" expr="['listening']"/>
    <!-- Turns. -->
    <data id="turn" expr="0"/>
    <data id="focused_device" expr="null"/>
    <data id="stimulus" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Who took part in the turn's stimulus, as its producer stamped them
         (the original's f6c4e08); a device's bot.input names no one. -->
    <data id="participants" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="focus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus_candidates" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The turn's choices, its output, and the output selection being
         sent (the <foreach> item). -->
    <data id="body_choices" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="choices" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="choices_over" expr="false"/>
    <data id="choices_size" expr="0"/>
    <data id="selections" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="s" expr="null"/>
    <data id="degraded_reason" expr="null"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="floppy.js"/>

  <state id="live" initial="activating">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="live_run" expr="nextLiveRun()"/>
      <assign location="offers" expr="({})"/>
      <assign location="waiting" expr="expectedAbilities()"/>
      <assign location="devices" expr="heldDevices()"/>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <!-- The original _clear_focus on every reboot and deactivate. -->
      <assign location="focused_device" expr="null"/>
    </onexit>
    <invoke id="cognition" type="scxml" src="../../abilities/cognition/cognition.scx">
      <param name="model" expr="model"/>
      <param name="bounds" expr="bounds"/>
      <param name="database" expr="database"/>
    </invoke>
    <invoke id="communication" type="scxml" src="../../abilities/communication/communication.scx">
      <param name="database" expr="database"/>
      <param name="environment" expr="environment"/>
    </invoke>
    <invoke id="identity" type="scxml" src="../../abilities/identity/identity.scx">
      <param name="database" expr="database"/>
    </invoke>
    <invoke id="listening" type="scxml" src="../../abilities/listening/listening.scx"/>
    <invoke id="stm" type="scxml" src="../../abilities/stm/stm.scx">
      <param name="database" expr="database"/>
    </invoke>
    <invoke id="persona" type="scxml" src="../../abilities/persona/persona.scx">
      <param name="database" expr="database"/>
      <param name="traits" expr="traits"/>
    </invoke>

    <!-- Each ability's latest offers; the first of a run is its readiness. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.offers" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.offers.json">
      <assign location="offers[_event.data.ability]" expr="_event.data.choices"/>
      <if cond="isWaiting(_event)">
        <assign location="waiting" expr="waitingWithout(_event)"/>
      </if>
    </transition>
    <!-- The cognition asks the identity for the bot's own name, and the
         identity's answer (also sent after each adoption) goes back to
         the cognition (the original's AskEvent and NamedEvent), from the
         start of each run: the cognition may ask while the bot is
         activating, and the identity answers once it knows. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.identity.ask" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.identity.ask.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.identity.ask" target="#_identity">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.identity.named" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.identity.named.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.identity.named" target="#_cognition">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <!-- The short-term register (the original's bot.register, reached by
         message only): the turns its producers write, and the answer to
         the body's read of them, for the cognition. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.turn" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.turn.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.memory.stm.turn" target="#_stm">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.output" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.output.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.output" target="#_cognition">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <!-- Nothing asks for the register's stimuli yet. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent.output" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent.output.json"/>
    <!-- What the bot knows of itself (the persona tells it on waking, while
         the bot may still be activating, and after each revision) goes to
         the cognition. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.persona.output" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.persona.output.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.persona.output" target="#_cognition">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.deactivate" event:schema="schemas/bot.deactivate.json" target="deactivating"/>
    <!-- A reboot (the cognition asks for one): re-enter live. -->
    <transition event="bot.reboot" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.reboot.json" target="live">
      <send event="bot.reboot" target="#_parent">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>

    <state id="activating">
      <onentry>
        <send id="activation-timer" event="activating.after" delayexpr="delay(activation_timeout_ms)">
          <param name="run" expr="live_run"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="activation-timer"/>
      </onexit>
      <transition cond="everyAbilityReady()" target="active">
        <send event="bot.activated" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="emptyData()"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="activating.after" cond="isCurrentRun(_event)" target="inactive">
        <log label="floppy.diagnostic" expr="activationTimeoutDiagnostic()"/>
        <send event="bot.activating.failed" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="emptyData()"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.*" target="inactive">
        <log label="floppy.diagnostic" expr="activatingErrorDiagnostic(_event)"/>
        <send event="bot.activating.failed" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="emptyData()"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="done.invoke" target="inactive">
        <log label="floppy.diagnostic" expr="activatingDoneDiagnostic(_event)"/>
        <send event="bot.activating.failed" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="emptyData()"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- The original's activation_cancelling (a2cbaa8): every accepted
           bot.deactivate is answered, so leaving live cancels the
           abilities and deactivating answers bot.deactivated. -->
      <transition event="bot.deactivate" event:schema="schemas/bot.deactivate.json" target="deactivating"/>
    </state>

    <state id="active" initial="unfocused">
      <!-- An ability that ends while the bot is active leaves it degraded. -->
      <transition event="done.invoke.cognition done.invoke.communication done.invoke.identity done.invoke.listening done.invoke.stm done.invoke.persona" target="degraded">
        <assign location="degraded_reason" expr="abilityEndedReason(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <!-- Communication input from outside goes to the communication, whose
           conversation answers with a product (a turn's stimulus, below),
           and to the identity, which answers when it names the bot. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.communication.input" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.communication.input.json">
        <send event="bot.ability.communication.input" target="#_communication">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
        <send event="bot.ability.communication.input" target="#_identity">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- A sound the environment delivers (the bot's own speech
           included): recorded in the short-term register, then a
           stimulus for every input ability. -->
      <transition event="environment.sound" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/environment.sound.json">
        <memory:stm_projection location="stm_payload" data="_event.data"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.memory.stm.record" target="#_stm">
          <content expr="stmRecord('environment.sound', _event)"/>
        </send>
        <foreach array="input" item="ability">
          <send event="environment.sound" targetexpr="abilityTarget(ability)">
            <content expr="_event.data"/>
          </send>
        </foreach>
      </transition>
      <!-- A visual stimulus is recorded in the short-term register, then
           goes to every input ability. -->
      <transition event="environment.visual" event:schema="schemas/environment.visual.json">
        <memory:stm_projection location="stm_payload" data="_event.data"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.memory.stm.record" target="#_stm">
          <content expr="stmRecord('environment.visual', _event)"/>
        </send>
        <foreach array="input" item="ability">
          <send event="environment.visual" targetexpr="abilityTarget(ability)">
            <content expr="_event.data"/>
          </send>
        </foreach>
      </transition>
      <!-- Speaking's playout: the efference copy goes only to Listening,
           before the sound (above). -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.speaking.efference.json">
        <foreach array="listening_abilities" item="ability">
          <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" targetexpr="abilityTarget(ability)">
            <content expr="_event.data"/>
          </send>
        </foreach>
      </transition>
      <!-- What the communication said, and its failures. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.output" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.speaking.output.json">
        <send event="bot.ability.speaking.output" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.communication.failed" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.communication.failed.json">
        <send event="bot.ability.communication.failed" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.conversation.failed.json">
        <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- A conversation product that is not text (the original's bot grants no
           turn for it). -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.output" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.conversation.output.json">
        <send event="bot.ability.conversation.output" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- What the listening could not hear. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.listening.failed" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.listening.failed.json">
        <send event="bot.ability.listening.failed" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- The body's own choices (the original: focus on active, clear only while
           a device is focused), offered on processing entry and taken as a
           stage sends them (one that no longer applies, a second clear in
           one turn, is ignored, as the original's guard ignores it). -->
      <transition event="bot.focus_device" event:schema="schemas/bot.focus_device.json"
                  cond="focusDeviceEnabled()">
        <if cond="isFocusCandidate(_event)">
          <assign location="focused_device" expr="_event.data.device"/>
          <log label="floppy.focus" expr="focused_device"/>
        </if>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.clear_focus" event:schema="schemas/bot.clear_focus.json"
                  cond="hasFocusedDevice()">
        <assign location="focused_device" expr="null"/>
        <log label="floppy.focus" expr="'none'"/>
      </transition>

      <state id="unfocused">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="focused_device" expr="null"/>
        </onentry>
        <transition event="bot.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.input.json" target="processing">
          <assign location="stimulus" expr="({})"/>
          <assign location="stimulus.event" expr="_event.name"/>
          <assign location="stimulus.data" expr="_event.data"/>
          <assign location="stimulus.source" expr="null"/>
          <assign location="participants" expr="[]"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.input" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.cognition.input.json" target="processing">
          <assign location="stimulus" expr="_event.data.stimulus"/>
          <assign location="participants" expr="handoffParticipants(_event)"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <state id="focused">
        <transition event="bot.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.input.json" target="processing">
          <assign location="stimulus" expr="({})"/>
          <assign location="stimulus.event" expr="_event.name"/>
          <assign location="stimulus.data" expr="_event.data"/>
          <assign location="stimulus.source" expr="null"/>
          <assign location="participants" expr="[]"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.input" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.cognition.input.json" target="processing">
          <assign location="stimulus" expr="_event.data.stimulus"/>
          <assign location="participants" expr="handoffParticipants(_event)"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- One turn of the cognition. -->
      <state id="processing">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="turn" expr="nextTurn()"/>
          <!-- The turns heard and said lately, for the cognition. -->
          <send event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns" target="#_stm">
            <content expr="emptyData()"/>
          </send>
          <cognition:attention_bias_for_turn location="focus_candidates" focuslocation="focus"
                                             stimulus="stimulus" devices="devices" focus="focused_device"/>
          <assign location="device_snapshots" expr="({})"/>
        </onentry>
        <!-- The live state of every held device (decision D109): the
             focused one's events are choices of this turn, and every read
             is the turn's environment (decision D106). A device whose
             session is not running is not read (<device:snapshot> assigns
             nothing), so it is left out. -->
        <onentry>
          <foreach array="devices" item="device">
            <device:snapshot location="device_snapshots[device]" target="deviceTarget(device)"/>
          </foreach>
        </onentry>
        <onentry>
          <decision:choice location="body_choices" events="bot.focus_device bot.clear_focus"/>
          <decision:pin location="body_choices" event="bot.focus_device" property="device" values="focus_candidates"/>
          <!-- bound: 32 KiB, the failure message below names it. -->
          <processing:collect_offered_events location="choices" choices="body_choices" offers="turnOffers()"
                                             devices="device_snapshots" focus="focused_device"
                                             bound="32768" overlocation="choices_over" sizelocation="choices_size"/>
          <log label="floppy.choices" expr="choices"/>
          <if cond="choicesFit()">
            <send event="bot.ability.cognition.input" target="#_cognition">
              <content expr="cognitionInput()"/>
            </send>
            <send id="processing-timer" event="bot.processing.timed_out" delayexpr="delay(processing_timeout_ms)">
              <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
            </send>
          </if>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="processing-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <!-- The choices do not fit: the turn fails before the cognition. -->
        <transition cond="choices_over" target="returning">
          <send event="bot.processing.failed" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="choicesOverFailure()"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <!-- The turn's output: its stages have sent their selections; the
             body sends itself those that name no target (the trusted
             seed's). -->
        <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.output" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.cognition.output.json"
                    cond="isCurrentTurn(_event)" target="returning">
          <log label="floppy.output" expr="botOutput(_event)"/>
          <assign location="selections" expr="_event.data.output"/>
          <send event="bot.processing.completed" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="processingCompleted()"/>
          </send>
          <foreach array="selections" item="s">
            <if cond="hasNoTarget(s)">
              <send eventexpr="s.event" target="#_internal">
                <content expr="selectionData(s)"/>
              </send>
            </if>
          </foreach>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.failed.json"
                    cond="isCurrentTurn(_event)" target="returning">
          <send event="bot.processing.failed" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="cognitionFailure(_event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.processing.timed_out" event:schema="schemas/bot.processing.timed_out.json"
                    cond="isCurrentTurn(_event)" target="cancelling_processing">
          <send event="bot.processing.timed_out" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="turnData()"/>
          </send>
          <send event="bot.ability.cognition.cancel" target="#_cognition">
            <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.input.json">
          <event:defer/>
          <log label="floppy.deferred" expr="_event.name"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.input" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.cognition.input.json">
          <event:defer/>
          <log label="floppy.deferred" expr="_event.name"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- The turn timed out: wait (bounded) for the cognition's
           acknowledgement of the cancel. -->
      <state id="cancelling_processing">
        <onentry>
          <send id="cancel-timer" event="bot.processing.cancel.timed_out"
                delayexpr="cancelDelay()">
            <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="cancel-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.cancelled" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.cognition.cancelled.json"
                    cond="isCurrentTurn(_event)" target="returning">
          <send event="bot.processing.failed" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="cancelledFailure()"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.processing.cancelled" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.processing.cancelled.json"
                    cond="isCurrentTurn(_event)" target="returning">
          <send event="bot.processing.failed" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="cancelledFailure()"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.processing.cancel.timed_out" event:schema="schemas/bot.processing.cancel.timed_out.json"
                    cond="isCurrentTurn(_event)" target="degraded">
          <send event="bot.processing.cancel.timed_out" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="turnData()"/>
          </send>
          <send event="bot.processing.failed" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="cancelledFailure()"/>
          </send>
          <!-- The original's transition into degraded announces it. -->
          <send event="bot.degraded" target="#_parent">
            <param name="stage" expr="'processing_cancel'"/>
          </send>
          <assign location="degraded_reason" expr="cancelUnacknowledgedReason()"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.input.json">
          <event:defer/>
          <log label="floppy.deferred" expr="_event.name"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.input" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.cognition.input.json">
          <event:defer/>
          <log label="floppy.deferred" expr="_event.name"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Back to attention: focused when a device is focused. -->
      <state id="returning">
        <transition cond="hasFocusedDevice()" target="focused"/>
        <transition target="unfocused"/>
      </state>

      <!-- A reply that belongs to no current turn is dropped. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.output bot.ability.cognition.cancelled bot.ability.processing.cancelled">
        <log label="floppy.stale" expr="staleReplyLog(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <!-- A failure that is no current turn's reply: the identity's, or
           the cognition's for another turn. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../../abilities/schemas/bot.ability.failed.json">
        <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
    </state>
  </state>

  <!-- Leaving live cancelled every ability. -->
  <state id="deactivating">
    <transition target="inactive">
      <send event="bot.deactivated" target="#_parent">
        <content expr="emptyData()"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- The bot left its environment (decision D107): a failed activation or
       bot.deactivate ends its session here. Nothing activates it again;
       rejoining is the environment invoking it again. -->
  <final id="inactive"/>

  <!-- A sink: the cognition did not acknowledge a cancel, or ended while
       active. The bot takes no more turns. The original's degraded is a state
       with no way out; here it is a top-level final state (scx validate
       refuses a state that can never exit, LINT002), so the session ends
       with the reason as its result. -->
  <final id="degraded">
    <onentry>
      <log label="floppy.degraded" expr="degraded_reason"/>
    </onentry>
    <donedata>
      <param name="reason" expr="degraded_reason"/>
    </donedata>
  </final>
</scxml>
